    "body": "Progress (issue-worker-max): three commits on `issue/532-wire-contour` (local, stacked on PR #560's head, `origin/main` merged in), quick gate running on the final head before the push.\n\n- `023324e0` generator in `crates/motion/src/wire_edm/`: the wire-centre path is the profile's mitred parallel at wire radius + gap, inside for a die and outside for a punch; straight lead from the stated start hole and back; the corner minimum and the start hole refused by name.\n- `fc7ab7c9` the Wire Contour operation in `crates/app` (kind id 41, its own Wire EDM section and family): a missing condition, gap or wire diameter is refused at command creation through #531's `Edm::condition`; the op mounts no library tool (the condition table is the wire's one source); stamp, machine check, post refusal, project file, two CL goldens.\n- `cded9490` a minimal page for the kind (the UI's tab law needs every kind's sections drawn), registry pins, `docs/decisions/532-wire-contour.md`.\n\nReadings (synthetic condition: wire 0.250, gap 0.040): die path 0.165 inside the profile, punch path 0.165 outside, apart 0.330 = the kerf width. A sharp rectangle as a die is refused (\"minimum inside radius is 0.1650 mm\"); the same rectangle as a punch is cut.\n\nFollow-ups filed: #1108 (MCP: wire contour op), #1109 (open-profile contour), #1110 (program sim, setup sheet and tool list on a tool-less wire cut).\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
